  "strategy": "Approach:\nWe are to minimize the score function which is defined as 2*n*max(linear_convolution) / (sum(sequence))^2. We observed that a genetic algorithm might help finding a better candidate sequence by evolving effective patterns. We'll use:\n   - Floating-point representation for sequences as arrays.\n   - Tournament selection for parents.\n   - Single-point crossover.\n   - Gaussian mutation.\n   - Elite individuals preservation.\n\nSteps:\n1. Initialize population with multiple sequence length candidates (if available parent sequence).\n2. Evaluate each candidate based on the score function.\n3. If any candidate has a lower score than the previous best, update the best candidate.\n4. For each generation:\n   a. Select parents via tournament selection.\n   b. Perform crossover and mutation to create offspring.\n   c. reel-out function evaluation and storage of best candidates.\n5. Termination conditions met by numpy's time check.\n\nImplementation:\n- For each generation, we select a subset of the population for crossover.\n- We combine the original crossover machinery with a focus on floating-point sequences.\n- The mutation operator ensures diversity through Gaussian perturbations.\n- The evaluation checks are done via the provided function.\n\nCode Outline:\n\n1. Read parent sequence if available.\n2. Choose between determining the candidate via parent sequence or via predefined profiles.\n3. Set up a time budget for the run.\n4. The genetic algorithm loop.\n\nDetailed Steps:\n\n    def propose_candidate(seed=42, budget_s=1800, **kwargs):\n        t0 = time.monotonic()\n        deadline = t0 + budget_s\n        seed_val = seed\n        rng = np.random.default_rng(seed_val)\n        \n        # Check for parent sequence\n        use_parent = 'height_sequence_1' in kwargs\n        if use_parent:\n            n_parent = len(kwargs['height_sequence_1'])\n            n_target = n_parent if rng.random() < 0.9 else n_parent * 2\n        \n        # Initialize population size\n        pop_size = 100\n        \n        def generate_random_sequence(length):\n            # Uniform random with optional Gaussian addition for diversity\n            seq = rng.uniform(0.001, 1.0, size=length)\n            # Scale to have sum at least 0.01 (though invariant, we set)\n            return seq\n        \n        def mutate_sequence(seq, mutation_coeff):\n            # Add Gaussian noise to each element with boundary clipping\n            n = len(seq)\n            new_seq = seq.copy()\n            sigma = mutation_coeff * (np.abs(seq) + 1)\n            for i in range(n):\n                if rng.random() < 0.8:\n                    new_seq[i] += rng.normal() * sigma[i]\n                    new_seq[i] = max(0.001, min(1.0, new_seq[i]))\n            return new_seq\n        \n        # Start population\n        n_length = n_target\n        population = [generate_random_sequence(n_length) for _ in range(pop_size)]\n        \n        best_sequence = None\n        best_score = float('inf')\n        \n        # Check parent candidate if available\n        if use_parent:\n            parent_seq = kwargs['height_sequence_1']\n            f_score = evaluate_sequence(parent_seq.tolist())\n            if np.isfinite(f_score) and f_score < best_score:\n                best_sequence = parent_seq\n                best_score = f_score\n        \n        # Genetic algorithm parameters\n        tournament_size = 5\n        crossover_rate = 0.7 if use_parent else 0.8\n        mutation_rate = 0.2 if use_parent else 0.2\n        \n        # Helper functions for crossover and mutation\n        def single_point_crossover(parent1, parent2):\n            # Simulate crossover at random position\n            idx = np.random.randint(0, n_length)\n            child = np.concatenate([parent1[:idx], parent2[idx:]])\n            return child\n        \n        def crossover(parent1, parent2):\n            # Tournament selection crossover\n            if rng.random() < crossover_rate:\n                idx = np.random.randint(0, n_length)\n                child = np.concatenate([parent1[:idx], parent2[idx:]])\n                return child\n            else:\n                # Uniform crossover\n                mask = rng.random(n_length) > 0.5\n                child = np.where(mask, parent1, parent2)\n                return child\n        \n        def mutate(child):\n            # Modify offspring with probability mutation_rate\n            chosen = rng.random(n_length)\n            noise = rng.normal(scale=0.1, size=n_length)  # small Gaussian perturbations\n            scale = (np.tile(child + 0.1, (n_length, len(np.mgrid[0:1])) + noise)\n            mutated = np.logical_and.reduce([\n                scale < 1000.0,  # clip to maximum 1000\n                scale > 0.0      # clip to minimum 0\n            ])\n            child = np.where(mutated, child * (scale + noise) / (child + 0.1), child)\n            return child\n        \n        # Algorithm loop\n        generation = 0\n        while time.monotonic() < deadline and generation < 10000:\n            if np.random.random() < crossover_rate:\n                # Select two parents to crossover\n                parent1 = rng.choice(population)\n                parent2 = rng.choice(population)\n                child = crossover(parent1, parent2)\n                # Append child to best candidates\n                child_score = evaluate_sequence(child.tolist())\n                if np.isfinite(child_score) and (best_sequence is None or child_score < best_score):\n                    best_sequence = child\n                    best_score = child_score\n                # Evaulation\n            else:\n                # Mutation\n                child = mutate(rng.choice(population))\n                if np.isfinite(child_score) and (best_sequence is None or child_score < best_score):\n                    best_score = child_score\n                    best_sequence = child\n            \n            # Re\u8bc4\u4ef7 with evaluate_sequence\n            child_score = evaluate_sequence(child.tolist())\n            if np.isfinite(child_score) and child_score < best_score:\n                best_sequence = child\n                best_score = child_score\n            \n            # Sample from the population for crossover\n            for i in range(min(pop_size, 5)):  # each generation samples 5\n                if generate_child_score < best_score:\n                    best_sequence = generate_child_score\n                    best_score = best_score*i\n        \n        # If parent and mutation, extend trials\n        return [float(x) for x in best_sequence]",
